From da5347a33f7eb557f3ae8b77c82e666952a5756f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: horizon-prism <horizon-prism@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:24:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: manage Horizon versions (M7)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- HorizonRelease parses what `horizon-launcher` prints with --json:
  versions (tag, name, date, prerelease, available_here, installed),
  versions --installed (installed, selected), update --check (horizon,
  launcher, launcher_current) and install (installed, prepared);
- HorizonInstance::launcherCli() finds the official CLI through
  launcherPath in horizon.json, Horizon.app on macOS, or PATH;
- HorizonVersionsDialog lists installed and available versions, refreshes
  on demand, installs, removes, checks for updates and hands a version to
  the settings page; it never touches the network on open, never removes
  a version Horizon or an instance plays, and never updates the launcher
  itself;
- HorizonSettingsPage gains a "Manage Horizon versions…" button; the
  chosen version fills the page's combos so apply() stays the only writer;
- HorizonRelease_test covers the four answers and their error cases
  (14 tests).

The CLI reports errors with exit code 1 and `error:` on stderr, and only
prints install progress when stderr is a terminal, so the dialog uses an
indeterminate bar and the exit code.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
